    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0241" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/9184: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-25T20:00:00+00:00"
                            >November 25, 1918—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 25—6:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>172. Secret for the President. My number 126, your number 59 and my number
                        159.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d158-f1"/> I have received no definite assurances
                    respecting number of delegates, but I now feel satisfied from informal
                    expression which I have received from both French and British authorities that
                    there will be no objection to the number being fixed. Accordingly, I modify my
                    suggestion contained in my number 126 that no announcement be made concerning
                    our delegation until arbitrators are committed to a definite number. I now see
                    no reason why you should not make whatever announcement you have in mind
                    respecting our delegates.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
